<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Jennings</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 1715–1720</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Jennings was an English privateer and pirate based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jamaica">Jamaica</a> and the Bahamas. In 1716 he raided the Spanish salvage camps of the wrecked 1715 treasure fleet off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, and he became one of the leading captains of the pirate community at Nassau. He accepted the royal pardon offered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodes-rogers">Woodes Rogers</a> in 1718, helping to end the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">Pirates</a>.</p></div>
